{"purpose":"Clarify Server Runtime domain for future planning: bootstrap, registry, registration, server command boundaries without changing completed sprint scope.","content":"PRD-001 Amendment 001: Server Runtime Context. Document ID PRD-001-AM-001, date 2026-07-25, status Accepted for future planning, effective Sprint 7. Preserves PRD-001 baseline while clarifying Server Runtime domain. Requirements R-1 Separate Execution Contexts (repo-aware Dev/CI vs repo-independent Server), R-2 Runtime Initialization (anvil server init under /etc/anvil), R-3 Runtime Registry (project ID under /etc/anvil/projects/{id}.yaml), R-4 Project Registration (anvil server project register, metadata-only, uniqueness), R-5 Server-Scoped Release Operations (resolve roots from Registry, artifact without cwd), R-6 Identity Validation (project ID shared between repo/artifact/registry). Scope: bootstrap/registration/boundaries, not provisioning/SSH/CI/supervision/secrets. Traceability ADR-013, MVP-001-AM-001. See docs/prd/PRD-001-amendment-001-server-runtime.md."}